@*
    A disabled member (confirmed their email before, then disabled by an administrator). Generic on purpose: no
    reason and no verify-email prompt, since confirming the email again doesn't re-enable the account.
*@
<div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert" test-id="accountDisabledMessage">
    <h4 class="alert-heading">You can't sign in</h4>
    <p class="mb-0">
        You can't sign in to this account. Please <a href="/support/feedback" class="alert-link">send us a message</a>
        if you think this is a mistake.
    </p>
</div>
